{"name":"get_network_references","title":"Get Network References","description":"Get all resources referencing a network — useful before deleting to check dependencies.

Returns {referenceResources: [...]}, one entry per resource type that references the
network; each entry is returned as {resourceType, referenceCount, references: [...]}
and each reference as {referenceId}. resourceType is one of CLIENT, DEVICE,
STATIC_ROUTE, OSPF_ROUTE, NEXT_AI, WIFI, NAT_RULE or SD_WAN (the pinned enum);
referenceCount is how many resources of that type reference it, and referenceId is
the id of one of them. The body is passed through as the console sent it.

The console may return HTTP 500 for some networks; this is an upstream condition.

Example call (get_network_references):
    {
      "host": "my-console",
      "site": "Default",
      "network_id": "3fa85f64-5717-4562-b3fc-2c963f66afa6"
    }","inputSchema":{"additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"host":{"type":"string","description":"Console name (case-insensitive reportedState.hostname/name, e.g. "my-console") or data[].id (MAC:numericId), from list_hosts. Serves Network and Protect."},"site":{"type":"string","description":"Network site name or UUID; resolved server-side. Get it from list_local_sites (name or
id). Names like "Default" work."},"network_id":{"type":"string","description":"Network/VLAN UUID. Get it from list_networks (data[].id). Network-app UUID — not
a Protect id."}},"required":["host","site","network_id"],"type":"object"},"annotations":{"readOnlyHint":true,"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":true,"openWorldHint":true},"_meta":{"unifi/apiSource":"network/official/read","fastmcp":{"tags":[]}}}

